{
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 5.08,
   "text": " You shit your pants, but you're a genius, so you rinse your underwear in water."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.64,
   "end": 10.52,
   "text": " But all this does is make it wet and smelly, so you add detergent and scrub it by hand."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.96,
   "end": 14.52,
   "text": " That works, but washing all your clothes yourself will take forever,"
  },
  {
   "start": 14.96,
   "end": 20.54,
   "text": " so you bring in 100 people to do it for you. But they want to be paid, so you get rid of them"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.54,
   "end": 24.36,
   "text": " and instead put everything inside a metal drum and turn it. Clever!"
  },
  {
   "start": 24.84,
   "end": 28.88,
   "text": " But your arm is still tired from earlier activities, so you add a motor."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.88,
   "end": 33.86,
   "text": " Now the drum turns itself, occasionally changing direction so the clothes don't get tangled."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.26,
   "end": 39.18,
   "text": " But now they're marinating in their own dirty water, so you put holes in the drum and a tub"
  },
  {
   "start": 39.18,
   "end": 44.06,
   "text": " around it to catch the water, then pump it away. Clean water comes in to rinse out the soap."
  },
  {
   "start": 44.48,
   "end": 47.66,
   "text": " Your underwear is finally clean, but it's still dripping,"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.08,
   "end": 51.36,
   "text": " so you spin the drum faster to throw the water out through the holes."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.82,
   "end": 54.48,
   "text": " Congratulations! You've invented the washing machine!"
  }
 ],
